Keywords for level 0 

1. POSIX compatibility layer / POSIX emulation layer (AKA Unix-like environment) — Compatibility layer: software that intercepts foreign API/syscalls, translates them into host OS calls, exposes a familiar interface (e.g., POSIX → Windows NT API), no hardware emulation, no guest OS, near-native performance.
2. Port — A 16-bit logical identifier (0–65535) that maps an incoming network packet to a specific process/socket on a Linux host. Pairs with an IP address to form a full socket address. Well-known ports (0–1023) are reserved for privileged services; higher ports are registered or ephemeral.
